  "term": "statistical stability",
  "definition": "Statistical stability is the quality of a set of measurements or markers showing consistent, reliable behavior across analyses. In this source, it is judged using coefficient of variation and correlation analyses, together with checking whether the findings remain meaningfully linked to the biological function being studied.",
